Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P7.7 Picking Claw / Snapping Claw steal on the killing blow

Techniques 127 (Picking Claw) and 128 (Snapping Claw) have the effect
TECH_EFFECT_STEAL. FIGHTSTG_startAction rolls it up front (FIGHTSTG_trySteal /
FIGHTSTG_rollSteal, which spends the random numbers and marks
FIGHTSTG_action.effects[TECH_EFFECT_STEAL]); the item moves to the bag, with
the "Stole <item>!" message, only when FIGHTSTG_updateActionEvents runs
(stealEnemyItem). FIGHTSTG_updateTechAction starts those events only when
task->step is 0, and dealTechDamage sets step to 1 when the hit leaves the
enemy at 0 HP (queueing its knock-out). So when the claw is the killing blow
the events are skipped: a steal the game already rolled as a success is
dropped without a message and the item stays on the enemy.

With a knocked-out target the port now starts the events anyway, after
clearing every effect except the steal (a status such as poison must not be
applied to a fighter that is down), and ends the action the way the
knock-out path does: no wake-up test and no counter motion (new substate 10
of FIGHTSTG_updateTechAction). The knock-out event is still queued first and
is handled by the battle menu once the action task is gone, so "Stole <item>!"
comes before "Defeated!" and stealEnemyItem still sees the fighter that was
hit. No random number is spent that was not spent before, and a steal that
did not succeed, or a claw that does not kill, runs exactly the old path.
The same TechData and code are on the US and EU discs. The player's first
technique (FIGHTSTG_updateFirstTech) has the same skip, but no partner has a
claw as skills[0] (only Growlmon, WarGrowlmon and the Digimon 369 learn them),
so it is left alone.

dw3-p77: log lines (stderr, PC) say when a steal happens and when it is the
knocked-out path.


--- a/src/battle/battle_mode/tech_action.c
+++ b/src/battle/battle_mode/tech_action.c
